{#- The colophon: a printer's mark at the foot of every page, carrying that
    page's own measurements.

    Why it exists. This site's whole competitive argument is that its claims
    are checkable — the work section publishes the counts that read as zero,
    the cases publish what shipped broken, the read time is derived from the
    text so it can never drift. Every one of those is the studio checking
    itself and then asking you to take the result on trust. This is the same
    move made visible: the figures the build measured, printed where the work
    ends, on the page they describe.

    It is a colophon in the literal sense — the note at the back of a book
    stating how it was made — and the mark is a registration target, the thing
    a printer aligns plates against to check the impression came out right.
    §5.3 of the direction record settled the ground on exactly that metaphor:
    a machinist's inspection plate and a printer's proof are the same object,
    a flat surface where you check whether something came out right.

    What is deliberately NOT here: the page's composite audit score. A score
    is an opinion the studio awarded itself, and publishing your own grade is
    weaker proof than publishing the measurements someone else can recompute.
    The numbers below are facts about the document you are reading.

    Mechanics. A native <details>, so it opens with a keyboard, is announced
    correctly, and works with JavaScript blocked — the §3.2 contract. The body
    is stamped after the build by scripts/colophon.mjs from the same payload
    scripts/audit.mjs emits, so there is exactly one definition of "words on
    this page". `data-audit-ignore` keeps the auditor from counting its own
    output as content. -#}
{%- set isEs = (L == "es") %}
      <aside class="colophon" data-audit-ignore aria-label="{{ "Colofón de la página" if isEs else "Page colophon" }}">
        <details class="colophon__details">
          <summary class="colophon__summary">
            <span class="colophon__mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" focusable="false">
                <circle class="colophon__mark-ring" cx="16" cy="16" r="10"/>
                <circle class="colophon__mark-dot" cx="16" cy="16" r="2.25"/>
                <path class="colophon__mark-cross" d="M16 1v9M16 22v9M1 16h9M22 16h9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <span class="colophon__label">{{ "Medido" if isEs else "Measured" }}</span>
            <span class="colophon__hint">{{ "Las cifras de esta página" if isEs else "This page, in figures" }}</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="colophon__body" data-colophon-body></div>
        </details>
      </aside>
